I have done this before.  

According to my crystal ball, you changed $GAME to nethack.exe.
This is useful for getting "make install" to find the game executable.
Unfortunately, it will then also name the shell script "nethack.exe",
and that shell script is what you are probably running to start the 
game.  I suppose then that Cygwin tries to treat it like a Windows 
executable file.  Why this causes the exact problem you are having (and 
I had) is unclear to me; but renaming the shell script will fix the 
problem.

If this isn't it, let me know, and I'll send you a diff.  Really, it
shouldn't take considerable fiddling to get it to compile (well---once
you find the STRNCMPI define).  Getting "make install" to work is the
only tricky part.

